        "notes": "Round Three\n\n[Crepuscular Circle](item_c0b93ed2-b692-44d5-a38a-ce5a63e83cdb) is going to change your playstyle for the rest of the match.\n\nI grab [Mid-Air Mobilizer](item_760c1441-8cfa-426c-885d-8d0dec32e145) here since it will help us out in Valk. Most of the time, I can't afford to grab a rare ability here, if you can, grab [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124) but only if you can afford it without selling anything else. I like to have all 6 abilities filled. \n\nIf you want, you can swap  [Icy Coolant](item_8b1c21e9-33e8-49a6-8277-a3a06d55a65f) for  [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) \n\nSometimes I sell  [Armored Vest](item_358361e2-59be-4c81-b221-8a87f37809e6) for another rare WP ability but only if surviving has been easy thus far. I will only grab a rare survival ability if I am really personally struggling to live but that does not happen often.\n\nTips:\n- Your pistol should have a 100% uptime during Valk, you have both beams auto connected to your team AND you have unlimited ammo so do not stop shooting! (It took me a long time to get used to this! 8+ years of muscle memory from regular Overwatch was hard to adjust...)\n- Try to focus squishy targets in valk\n- In valk, stay within range with your team so they can benefit from the double beams, don't go too far\n- You should *prioritize* healing to build your ult fast and as often as you can. But you can and should still blue beam when your team is mostly full health, especially in these earlier rounds. But in late game, you won't really have time for it.\n- Ults charge fast in Stadium, so use valk quickly after getting it (Except for down times/respawning/after fights are mostly finished)\n- Don't feel discouraged if you are not able to get kills with your ult, your beams are doing the most to support your team here! It can be really hard to secure a kill in later rounds, but just keep shooting.",
